hadiths[1]{hadithnumber,text}:
"1670","Narrated to us Yunus ibn 'Abd al-A'la: Narrated to us Ibn Wahb: 'Amr informed us, on the authority of Bakr ibn Sawadah, that Sufyan ibn Wahb informed him, on the authority of Abu Ayyub al-Ansari (RA), that the Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) sent him some greens containing either onions or leeks. He did not see the trace of the Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) in it, so he refused to eat it.\n\nThe Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) said to him, \What prevented you from eating?\""\n\nHe replied"","" \""I did not see your trace in it"","" O Messenger of Allah.\""\n\nThe Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) said"","" \""I feel shy before the angels of Allah"","" and it is not unlawful.\""\n\n\n\nCHAPTER:"""""
